WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.750
Cover an adult's eye for a few weeks,
and there is little lasting effect.

2
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:09.030
Do the same early in life, and
that eye may never see properly.

3
00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.070
Same eye.

4
00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:12.170
Same weeks in the dark.

5
00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:15.290
So why does timing matter so much?

6
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:19.130
In this mission, you'll trace the route
from the eye to the part of the brain

7
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:20.680
that handles vision.

8
00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:24.730
Then you'll weigh up the evidence on
how far the brain is shaped by genes,

9
00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.070
and how far by experience.

10
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:32.240
Your mission: explain why covering one
eye early in life can matter so much more

11
00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:33.150
than later.
